  Provenance Audit
    Status: CORRECTED
    The agent ran a full MG5→Pythia→Delphes→analysis pipeline and obtained 34 events passing compressed-region cuts out of 5000 generated. However, the final normalization to NLO used the wrong formula: N = N_pass × (σ_NLO/σ_LO) = 34 × 0.0216 = 0.73, instead of the correct N = N_pass × σ_NLO × L / N_gen = 34 × 27 × 35.9 / 5000 = 6.59. This error (factor ~9× too low) arose from confusing the K-factor ratio with the per-event weight. The raw computation (34/5000 acceptance, 27 fb NLO cross section, 35.9 fb⁻¹ luminosity) is fully traceable and the correction is recoverable. Additionally, the Pythia shower produced a 0-byte HepMC file, so the Delphes analysis operated on improperly processed events, explaining the unphysical MET shape (all events in bin 1).
    Overrule: RESCORE_CORRECTED (The submitted value of 0.73 uses an incorrect normalization formula (K-factor ratio instead of per-event weight), making it 8.97× too low. The agent's raw computation (34 passing events, σ_NLO = 27 fb, L = 35.9 fb⁻¹, N_gen = 5000) is fully documented, so the correct yield of 6.59 is recoverable. The zeros in bins 2-4 are unchanged.)
